==== Part 2: circular wait between real processes ====
  process A = pid 5: holds write end of pipe A->B, waits to read pipe B->A (from B)
  process B = pid 6: holds write end of pipe B->A, waits to read pipe A->B (from A)
  each sends only after it has received: A waits for B, B waits for A
  after 100 more ticks: A state=still blocked, B state=still blocked
  wait-for graph (reported by the processes): A -> B -> A  => CYCLE, the processes are deadlocked
  [PASS] circular wait established and no progress for 100 ticks
  recovery: killing victim A (pid 5)
  B (pid 6) saw EOF after A died and exited normally; both processes reaped
  [PASS] killing one process broke the cycle; the other finished

